WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.726
Idea. Two friends start a car-wash business. One puts in more money. The other works more hours. How should they share the profit? Without rules agreed at the start, they may argue.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:26.058
A partnership agreement is a written document of the rules the partners have agreed. It usually covers the profit-sharing ratio, interest on capital and on drawings, partners' salaries, and interest on partners' loans.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:43.353
If there is no agreement, section twenty-four of the Partnership Act of eighteen ninety applies. Profits and losses are shared equally. There are no salaries, no interest on capital, and no interest on drawings. A partner's loan earns five per cent a year.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:55.347
Method. For an advise question, make each point, then develop it: say what it leads to. Explain what happens without an agreement. Then end with a clear decision.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:08.859
The Act's rules can be unfair. Ali puts in thirty thousand and Bea ten thousand. Under the Act, a profit of twenty thousand is split ten thousand each, with no interest on Ali's extra capital.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:22.201
Worked example. Here is a real question from November 2024. Haitai and Ming did not draw up a formal partnership agreement. Advise them whether they should. Five marks.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:32.452
First point: an agreement sets out what each partner is entitled to and responsible for. So if they disagree, they can check the document to settle it.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:40.793
Second point: written terms stop arguments starting. Fewer arguments means business decisions can be made more quickly.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:54.053
Third point: without an agreement, the Partnership Act of eighteen ninety applies. Profits are shared equally, with no salary or interest on capital, even if one partner works or invests more.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:02:05.188
Decision: I advise Haitai and Ming to draw up a formal partnership agreement. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:15.770
Common mistake. A common mistake is thinking the Act gives five per cent interest on capital. The five per cent is only on partners' loans.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:21.971
Another is thinking the Act shares profit in the ratio of capital. It shares profit equally.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:31.627
Your turn. Now you try. Rosa and Kenji have no agreement. Use the Act to answer both parts. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:47.273
Answer. Profit is shared equally: eighteen thousand dollars each. There is no interest on capital, and no salaries. Only Kenji's loan earns interest: five per cent of ten thousand is five hundred dollars a year.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:56.457
Remember: know the Act's rules, develop each point with its effect, and end with a clear decision. Now try the practice questions.
